{"source_id":"arXiv:1712.03006","title":"Quantum Howe duality and invariant polynomials","abstract":"We construct two examples of q-deformed classical Howe dual pairs (sl(2,C), sl(2,C)) and (sl(2,C), sl(n,C)). Moreover, we obtain a noncommutative version of the first fundamental theorem of classical invariant theory. Our approach to these duality differs from the paper of Lehrer-Zhang-Zhang. Furthermore, we solve the tensor product decomposition problem for Verma modules over U_q(sl(2,C)) provided q is not a root of unity.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Libor Krizka","Jian Zhang"],"year":"2017","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1712.03006","doi":"10.48550/arXiv.1712.03006","cluster":"quantum_algebra","cards":[{"card_id":"ma-c-cbb9bd61870bda3edef1","label":"Abstract","kind":"abstract","line":282,"snippet":"We construct two examples of $q$-deformed classical Howe dual pairs $(\\mathfrak{sl}(2,\\mathbb{C}),\\mathfrak{so}(3,\\mathbb{C}))$ and $(\\mathfrak{sl}(2,\\mathbb{C}),\\mathfrak{sl}(n,\\mathbb{C}))$. …"},{"card_id":"ma-c-488a8cedb9010578d707","label":"Equation isomomorphism polynomials","kind":"equation","line":538,"snippet":"\\varphi_q(x^ay^bz^c)=x^az^cy^b"},{"card_id":"ma-c-2ef4637898e48d080a4f","label":"Equation standard rep","kind":"equation","line":925,"snippet":"\\begin{gathered} \\rho_{q,V}(E_i)=E_{i,i+1}, \\qquad \\rho_{q,V}(F_i)=E_{i+1,i}, \\\\ \\rho_{q,V}(K_i)=\\sum_{j=1}^{i-1} E_{j,j} + qE_{i,i}+q^{-1}E_{i+1,i+1} + \\sum_{j=i+2}^n E_{j,j} \\end{gathered} …"},{"card_id":"ma-c-01a4db280858aa5539ed","label":"Equation identification","kind":"equation","line":1025,"snippet":"\\C_q[V] \\otimes_\\C \\C_q[V^*] \\simeq \\C_q[x] \\otimes_\\C \\C_q[y] \\riso \\C_q[x,y]"},{"card_id":"ma-c-92b4b325f334cfac182e","label":"Equation sing vectors recurrence","kind":"equation","line":1417,"snippet":"a_k[k]_q[\\mu-k+1]_q+a_{k-1} q^{\\mu+2-2k}[n-k+1]_q[\\lambda-n+k]_q=0"},{"card_id":"ma-c-d7b4c14316cceb451570","label":"Equation short exact sequence","kind":"equation","line":1